  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Preface\nWhilst the discussion of age ratings and content filters has come up time and again, there has been a central, or rather, commonly reoccurring minimum consensus amongst the conversation **that for personal safety amidst the platform**, the bare minimum should be the allowance for age-based safety filters and instance gating.\nThe online landscape is rough, and there is an inherent level of liability when communicating in a space with minors present which may make use of VRChat services to the fullest **difficult** and uncertain.\nThis feedback is **not** about NSFW content, nor will it be. This is not suggesting the allowance of such content, which is for a different, [albeit related topic](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/age-verificationnsfw-content).\n \n# Birthdays\nSimilar to major social media platforms and game services like Steam, the simplest addition would be to add birthdays to user profiles, optionally.\nUsers with birthdays placing them **under the age of 13 at time of account creation** would be suspended pending review.\nUsers with birthdays placing them **over the age of 17 or 18** would be given additional safety and instance options.\nBirthdays could also be used for fun little effects and in-client treatment (confetti, a party hat, party blower, etc.)\nSaid feedback is **not** suggesting any form of data collection or verification beyond the voluntary entry of a birthdate.\n \n# Age-based Safety\nFor those over the appropriate age, an additional Safety rank would be added to the Safety settings menu.\nSaid setting would allow users to either \"inherit\" existing safety settings for those with a set birthdate that is under-age, or override it with custom safety options. This would allow a user to potentially, at it's strongest settings, auto-mute and disable the avatar of those underaged in their presence by default.\n \n# Gated Instances\nAbove-aged users with a set birthdate would be able to create, view, and join, \"gated\" instances, which would require a user to have a birthday on file and be above the required age to join.\n**Note:** If concerns about instance segregation by age are present, VRChat may limit this feature to private (Invite/Friends/+) instances only, with Public instances permanently E for Everyone, at their discretion.\n \n# Gated Worlds\nAdditionally, in order to comply with various laws, and to increase user safety, worlds may indicate that they may be unsuitable for minors. This could include worlds with themes of Alcohol, Strong Language, or others of adult nature which fall safe within VRChat's content guidelines, or which are otherwise designed for an adults-only audience.",
